      {
        "id": 153754,
        "name": "LACK OF SUBTLETY",
        "username": "LACK_OF_SUBTLETY",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/bcef8e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-21T20:28:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I personally find it incredibly confusing that if I \"Play\" a one-shot card, It is not considered to be \"in my play area\". Especially since the rules are clear on the fact that until it is resolved, it remains on the table in front of you before being moved to the trash.</p><p>It seems a simpler change would be for Kinetic Looter to read \"The first time a&nbsp;hero card other than a one-shot leaves play each turn...\" if that is the intention.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:33:08.904Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
